<Site title="Find reliable local information" description="A practical route to dated local weather, water service and quality information without invented contacts or universal advice.">
  <PageHeader title="Start with the right local record" eyebrow="Public information" description="A national rainfall figure cannot tell you whether your tap is running or safe. The useful next step depends on your place and the problem you are checking." />
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="grid-3"><article class="editorial-card story-step"><p class="eyebrow">If you need a weather or crop outlook</p><h3>Check the issue and validity dates.</h3><p>Use a current bulletin for your district or crop stage. A seasonal forecast is a forecast for its stated period, not a report of what has happened at a farm.</p><a href="https://mausam.imd.gov.in/imd_latest/contents/agromet/advisory/blocalmain.php">IMD agromet advisory portal ↗</a></article><article class="editorial-card story-step"><p class="eyebrow">If your supply is interrupted</p><h3>Find the provider for your service area.</h3><p>Check its dated notice for the affected streets, expected timing and official reporting channel. Keep the notice date and a record of the interruption if you are seeking a response. Our state pages are a starting place for evidence coverage, not a verified directory of every utility.</p><a href={url('/states/')}>Browse states and UTs ↗</a></article><article class="editorial-card story-step"><p class="eyebrow">If quality is in question</p><h3>Use the responsible local advisory.</h3><p>Rainfall, colour or a distant water test cannot establish the safety of a particular tap. Consult the current local water provider or public-health authority for its tested result and instructions. This site does not offer treatment or medical directions.</p><a href="https://jaljeevanmission.gov.in/sites/default/files/guideline/WQMS-Framework.pdf">JJM water-quality framework ↗</a></article></div>
    <div class="section-head story-rail"><div><p class="eyebrow">For a community or newsroom</p><h2>Ask one precise, answerable question.</h2></div><p>What changed, where, when, who measured it, and how was the response documented?</p></div><div class="grid-2"><div><h3>What to record</h3><ul><li>The named location and responsible water system, without publishing a vulnerable person's exact home.</li><li>The dates and wording of official notices, test reports or orders.</li><li>What residents report, clearly attributed and distinguished from measured service.</li></ul></div><div><h3>What to request</h3><ul><li>Service schedules, volume and quality results for the affected area.</li><li>Original orders, funds released, work completion and measured outcomes.</li><li>Changes over time, including restoration and remaining gaps.</li></ul></div></div><div class="note"><strong>Contacts need verification</strong><p>We have not verified a nationwide directory of local utility contacts or emergency numbers. A stale or wrong contact can waste time; use the current official notice for your place. <a href={url('/journalists/')}>See the document question bank ↗</a></p></div>
  </div></section>
</Site>
